<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The porch ~ the sweeper's kit

The operator ruled on 2026-10-26 to close open work before the founding bake. This lane sweeps the road's hygiene pile (burned-name guards, evergreen remainders, tests-only debts, re-measures and canon sweeps) beside the slotted lanes, in small trains: each bundle lands off the span head, and the controller writes the road at each land. The crew stands as <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm#/the-shapes">>: one walled Sol builder, one walled Luna reader and sweeper, the lead running every suite.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/bundle-one>>

!! Bundle one ~ three tooling items and the burned-name guards

!!! The Playwright engine cache
* ''A CDN stall once held a runner for 20 minutes and for 48.'' Every job in `.github/workflows` that installs engines (`ci.yml`'s browser-vessel suite, floor crossing and standalone single-file suite; `held-out.yml`'s browser-weld cell) now restores `~/.cache/ms-playwright` keyed on the runner OS, the Playwright version `pnpm exec playwright --version` names, and the engine set. The install step still runs for the system libraries and downloads only on a miss. A version bump re-downloads once.
* ''Stays.'' The TiddlyWiki5 submodule's own `bin/ci-test.sh` installs engines for upstream's CI, outside this repository's workflows.

!!! The household witness image
* ''`household-https-witness` builds `lares-surface:local` from this tree on every run'' when `HOUSEHOLD_IMAGE` stands unset, so a stale local tag never meets newer code (the layer cache keeps an unchanged tree cheap). A set `HOUSEHOLD_IMAGE` reads as given and builds only when the tag stands absent.
* ''Stays.'' `tools/harbor-walk-witness.sh` keeps the same absent-only build (`HARBOR_IMAGE`); it wants the same line when its next owner touches it.

!!! The `custody-frames` U1 leak
* ''The cause.'' U1's control read `loadActivePersonaIndex().catch(() => undefined)`. That reader infers the one face standing open, and it opens the seated custody, which refuses outside a scratch root. Under a real `HOME` the refusal fell into the `catch` and the assertion read green by accident; under a scratch `HOME` or `LAR_ROOT` the custody opened, an earlier vector's face stood open, and the reader answered `0`.
* ''The cure.'' The control reads the session's own choice (`wornFaceOrdinal()`), the thing the unlock frame sets, and the file reads green under a real `HOME` and under a scratch `HOME` with a scratch `LAR_ROOT`. The test title no longer claims a case it never asserted: an unlock naming no face wears the vessel's one face by the door's own rule.

!!! Burned-name guards burned
* `lar-wire.test.ts`: the control that `wiki:dom-event` and `wiki:dom-input` pass no door (road `F8`).
* `browser-walk.test.ts`: the control that the `boot-invite-burned`, `hosting-walk` and `nexus-keys` stores stand absent (road `W20`).
* `vessel-wipe-surfaces.test.ts`, now `vessel-surfaces.test.ts`: the `vessel clear`, `rite rebirth` and `--clear` refusals and the negative help checks; the live `read`, refresh and surface-table assertions stay.
* `nexus-verb-reach.test.ts`: `nexus refresh` reads as an unknown verb.
* `vault-door.test.ts`: the former vault verbs (`seal`, `rotate`, `repair`, `passphrase`, `export`), `--yes`, `--check` and the passphrase environment route; the exact seven-verb help assertion and a nonsense-verb refusal stay.
* `cabal-realm-ceremony.test.ts`: the absent-export list for the former eviction and closing API; the exact live export assertion stays.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/bundle-two>>

!! Bundle two ~ the stream manifest, the witness image, the leak and the readings

!!! Closed
* ''`G38` The stream manifest stands as one shape in both languages.'' The Python writer (`sensorium.py`) declares `lifecycle` in every stream manifest: it mirrors `deriveLifecycle` at mint, `set_stream_ephemeral` recomputes it when `ephemeral` flips, and a declared `tombstone` stays. The reader (`sensorium.ts`) requires a declared state and refuses an absent one by name; the derivation fallback burned. The builder keeps its mint-time default, which writes the field. Python tests pin the writer and the setter; the node tests pin the refusal beside its control.
* ''`tools/harbor-walk-witness.sh` builds from the tree'' with `HARBOR_IMAGE` unset, as the household witness does.
* ''The `held-out-steps` test names its actor.'' The plan test read `git config user.name`, which a scratch `HOME` lacks; it now names `GITHUB_ACTOR` as the runner does, and the file reads green under a scratch `HOME`.

!!! Readings, no change owed
* ''`H7`.'' No line in `membership-doctrine` calls an introduction's lifetime unruled any longer. `#/the-invite` states that the answer consumes the introduction, that the three dials count and read no clock, and that a posture names a setting and never a date. The strike belongs to the road.
* ''`G19` carriers read true against the code at this head.'' The five sweeps met no disagreeing line:
** `docker-compose.mesh.yml` and `docker-compose.browser-ci.yml` both state that the localhost exemption is not TLS and cite each other;
** `secure-context#/behind-the-terminator` and `harbor#/household-https` agree on `LAR_PUBLIC_URL`, loopback publication and the scheme;
** the test door's marker (`.lar-test-scratch`) and the suites' temp-dir check (`scratch-custody-setup.ts`) stand as two named things, and no carrier merges them.
* ''`kahu.mem` and `lamplighters.mem` on what the code holds'' needs a reader who holds the operator's intent for the cadence share. It stays on `G19` for the controller.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/rulings-owed>>

!! Rulings and builds owed, each with its lean

* ''`A9` the browser harness image.'' `docker-compose.browser-ci.yml`'s `qa` runner binds the repository read-only at `/repo` because the walks it runs (`tools/browser-ci-smoke.mjs`, `packages/lararium-web/tests/live-wiki.mjs`) import `playwright` and probe modules from the tree. Options: (1) a `browser-harness` Dockerfile target that bakes `tools/`, the probes and the web tests into a Playwright-based image, rebuilt per run; (2) the `probe-code` volume shape `harness-image-law` already allows for the mesh compose, filled from the product image; (3) keep the bind and name it in `harness-image-law`'s exceptions. Lean: (1), since a walk then proves the bytes of its image, but it moves where authors edit a walk, which is the operator's call.
* ''`G8` measures.'' No earlier per-verb flush reading or bench stands in the tree, so the re-measure has no instrument to name; it wants a bench written first. Pack-PIN recursion stays unbuilt (`blob-carriage#/proposed-law`). `assertBodyIndexTier` has no production caller because `bodyIndexBagUri` has no production producer (`holdings-witness.ts`): the caller arrives with the cad body-index writer. Lean: leave the three on `G8` with those reasons and build the caller with the writer.
* ''`G17` tests only.'' The closing review that named the mutation survivors does not stand in the tree or the log, so the survivors cannot be listed. The sealed suite shows no test of the node door's scratch-marker admission and rejection (`main.ts`, `.lar-test-scratch`). Lean: the controller names the review; the marker test is a bundle-three build.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/what-stays>>

!! What stays, and why

* ''`projection-input-leg.test.ts` (road `F8`).'' It guards `wiki:dom-event` and `wiki:dom-input` as unclaimed. It belongs to D2's tw5 projection test surface; it burns when D2 lands.
* ''The CLI unknown-command list and the keyhive cabal names (road `W20`).'' The unknown-command refusal is generic and tests with a nonsense control; no named cabal guard remains outside the held modules (`ceremony-core.ts`, `keyhive-provider.ts`, `boot-daemon-keyhive.ts`, K15).
* ''Bundle three.'' `G6` and `G20` come after bundle two, as the controller ordered.

<<~/ahu>>

